"Choose a workspace","nova.training.pebble-page-page:PlatformHubPage.body",u.tV,"nova.training.pebble-page-page:BusinessAcquisitionPage.title","Your acquisition workspace","nova.training.pebble-page-page:BusinessAcquisitionPage.body",u.ky,"nova.training.buyer-home-metric-0.title","Active deals","nova.training.buyer-home-metric-0.body",u.Ax,"nova.training.buyer-home-metric-1.title","Under review","nova.training.buyer-home-metric-1.body",u.ro,"nova.training.buyer-home-metric-2.title","Due soon","nova.training.buyer-home-metric-2.body",u.Dp,"nova.training.buyer-home-metric-3.title","Needs attention","nova.training.buyer-home-metric-3.body",u.EY,"nova.training.buyer-home-search.title","Find a deal in your pipeline","nova.training.buyer-home-search.body",u.zi,"nova.training.buyer-home-start.title","Bring an opportunity into the app","nova.training.buyer-home-start.body",u.ot,"nova.training.buyer-home-stage-0.title","Sourcing","nova.training.buyer-home-stage-0.body",u.EV,"nova.training.buyer-home-stage-1.title","Under review","nova.training.buyer-home-stage-1.body",u.EU,"nova.training.buyer-home-stage-2.title","LOI / diligence","nova.training.buyer-home-stage-2.body",u.iW,"nova.training.buyer-home-stage-3.title","Closing","nova.training.buyer-home-stage-3.body",u.ER,"nova.training.buyer-home-team.title","Your personal team","nova.training.buyer-home-team.body",u.L,"nova.training.buyer-input-businessName.title","Business name","nova.training.buyer-input-businessName.body","A name to identify this business deal. You can leave it blank. Example \u2192 Harbour Advisory.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessAsk.title","Asking price","nova.training.buyer-input-businessAsk.body","The seller\u2019s requested price for the business, before deal adjustments. Example \u2192 1,200,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessRevenue.title","Annual revenue","nova.training.buyer-input-businessRevenue.body","Total sales generated by the business in a typical year, before expenses. Example \u2192 1,800,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessEbitda.title","Reported EBITDA","nova.training.buyer-input-businessEbitda.body","Reported annual earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortization. Example \u2192 260,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessAddbacks.title","Verified add-backs","nova.training.buyer-input-businessAddbacks.body","One-time or owner-specific expenses you can verify in the records and add back to earnings. Example \u2192 0.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessOwnerComp.title","Owner compensation in EBITDA","nova.training.buyer-input-businessOwnerComp.body","Owner pay already included as an expense in reported EBITDA. Do not add it again if EBITDA already excludes it. Example \u2192 0.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessSalary.title","Replacement manager salary","nova.training.buyer-input-businessSalary.body","Annual pay and benefits needed to hire someone to replace the owner\u2019s work. Example \u2192 0.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessCapex.title","Annual maintenance investment","nova.training.buyer-input-businessCapex.body","Typical yearly spending to maintain equipment and other operating assets. Example \u2192 0.","nova.training.buyer-input-multipleLow.title","Low EBITDA multiple","nova.training.buyer-input-multipleLow.body","The lower comparable-sale multiple applied to maintainable EBITDA. Example \u2192 3.","nova.training.buyer-input-multipleHigh.title","High EBITDA multiple","nova.training.buyer-input-multipleHigh.body","The upper comparable-sale multiple applied to maintainable EBITDA. Example \u2192 5.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessDown.title","Down payment %","nova.training.buyer-input-businessDown.body","Percent of the asking price you plan to pay in cash at closing. Example \u2192 25.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessInterest.title","Interest %","nova.training.buyer-input-businessInterest.body","Annual interest rate assumed for the acquisition loan. Example \u2192 7.","nova.training.buyer-input-businessYears.title","Loan amortization (years)","nova.training.buyer-input-businessYears.body","Number of years over which the acquisition loan is paid down. Example \u2192 7.","nova.training.buyer-result-business.title","Read the business results","nova.training.buyer-result-business.body","The earnings bridge explains maintainable EBITDA. Multiples give an indicative price range, and the price gap compares it with the ask. Debt service, coverage and cash after debt depend on the financing assumptions and maintenance investment. Results appear when the required fields are complete.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetAsk.title","Asking price","nova.training.buyer-input-assetAsk.body","The seller\u2019s requested price for the assets in this deal. Example \u2192 850,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetEquipment.title","Equipment & vehicles","nova.training.buyer-input-assetEquipment.body","Current market value of equipment and vehicles included in the sale. Example \u2192 500,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetInventory.title","Saleable inventory","nova.training.buyer-input-assetInventory.body","Realistic sale value of usable inventory included in the deal. Example \u2192 180,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetReceivables.title","Collectible receivables","nova.training.buyer-input-assetReceivables.body","Customer amounts owed that you expect to collect and acquire. Example \u2192 120,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetIntangibles.title","Transferable intangibles","nova.training.buyer-input-assetIntangibles.body","Supportable value of transferable assets such as licenses, contracts or intellectual property. Example \u2192 100,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetCash.title","Cash included","nova.training.buyer-input-assetCash.body","Cash balances that transfer to you at closing. Example \u2192 40,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetLiabilities.title","Liabilities assumed","nova.training.buyer-input-assetLiabilities.body","Debts and other obligations you agree to take over. Example \u2192 150,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetMaintenance.title","Deferred maintenance","nova.training.buyer-input-assetMaintenance.body","Cost to repair or replace assets whose upkeep has been deferred. Example \u2192 30,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetCosts.title","Transaction costs","nova.training.buyer-input-assetCosts.body","Legal, appraisal, transfer and other costs of completing the purchase. Example \u2192 20,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-assetRecovery.title","Recovery rate %","nova.training.buyer-input-assetRecovery.body","Percent of noncash asset value you expect to recover in a quick sale. Example \u2192 60.","nova.training.buyer-result-assets.title","Read the asset results","nova.training.buyer-result-assets.body","The asset bridge adds included assets and cash, then subtracts liabilities and deferred maintenance. Compare adjusted net assets with the ask. Buyer cost includes transaction costs; the liquidation floor uses the recovery rate for noncash assets. Results appear when the required fields are complete.","nova.training.buyer-input-creName.title","Property name","nova.training.buyer-input-creName.body","A name to identify this property deal. You can leave it blank. Example \u2192 Main Street Plaza.","nova.training.buyer-input-creAsk.title","Asking price","nova.training.buyer-input-creAsk.body","The seller\u2019s requested purchase price for the property. Example \u2192 5,000,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-creRent.title","Annual potential rent","nova.training.buyer-input-creRent.body","Annual rent the property could earn if all rentable space paid as expected. Example \u2192 480,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-creOther.title","Annual other income","nova.training.buyer-input-creOther.body","Annual property income outside base rent, such as parking or storage. Example \u2192 20,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-creVacancy.title","Vacancy & credit loss %","nova.training.buyer-input-creVacancy.body","Percent of potential income lost to empty space and unpaid rent. Example \u2192 5.","nova.training.buyer-input-creExpenses.title","Operating expenses / year","nova.training.buyer-input-creExpenses.body","Annual property operating costs, excluding debt payments and income tax. Example \u2192 140,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-creReserve.title","Replacement reserve / year","nova.training.buyer-input-creReserve.body","Annual allowance for replacing major building components over time. Example \u2192 20,000.","nova.training.buyer-input-creCap.title","Market cap rate %","nova.training.buyer-input-creCap.body","Market capitalization rate used to convert stabilized net operating income into value. Example \u2192 6.","nova.training.buyer-input-creDown.title","Down payment %","nova.training.buyer-input-creDown.body","Percent of the property asking price you plan to pay in cash. Example \u2192 30.","nova.training.buyer-input-creInterest.title","Interest %","nova.training.buyer-input-creInterest.body","Annual interest rate assumed for the property loan. Example \u2192 6.5.","nova.training.buyer-input-creYears.title","Loan amortization (years)","nova.training.buyer-input-creYears.body","Number of years over which the property loan is paid down. Example \u2192 25.","nova.training.buyer-input-creHold.title","Holding period (years)","nova.training.buyer-input-creHold.body","Number of years you expect to own the property before selling. Example \u2192 5.","nova.training.buyer-input-creGrowth.title","Annual NOI growth %","nova.training.buyer-input-creGrowth.body","Expected yearly percentage change in net operating income. Example \u2192 2.","nova.training.buyer-input-creExitCap.title","Exit cap rate %","nova.training.buyer-input-creExitCap.body","Capitalization rate assumed when estimating the property\u2019s sale value. Example \u2192 6.5.","nova.training.buyer-result-realEstate.title","Read the property results","nova.training.buyer-result-realEstate.body","Potential income minus vacancy, operating costs and replacement reserves gives stabilized NOI. NOI divided by the market cap rate gives income value. Debt coverage and cash after debt use your financing terms; hold and exit assumptions drive the projected sale value and stress view. Results appear when the required fields are complete.","nova.training.seller-home-metric-0.title","Active transfers","nova.training.seller-home-metric-0.body",u.vQ,"nova.training.seller-home-metric-1.title","Plan complete","nova.training.seller-home-metric-1.body",u.eP,"nova.training.seller-home-metric-2.title","Due soon","nova.training.seller-home-metric-2.body",u.cj,"nova.training.seller-home-metric-3.title","Needs attention","nova.training.seller-home-metric-3.body",u.lS,"nova.training.seller-home-search.title","Find your transfer","nova.training.seller-home-search.body",u.dw,"nova.training.seller-home-start.title","Set up your transfer plan","nova.training.seller-home-start.body",u.df,"nova.training.seller-home-stage-0.title","Preparation","nova.training.seller-home-stage-0.body",u.d7,"nova.training.seller-home-stage-1.title","Successor search","nova.training.seller-home-stage-1.body",u.yY,"nova.training.seller-home-stage-2.title","Terms / diligence","nova.training.seller-home-stage-2.body",u.uT,"nova.training.seller-home-stage-3.title","Closing / handover","nova.training.seller-home-stage-3.body",u.od,"nova.training.seller-home-team.title","Your personal team","nova.training.seller-home-team.body",u.L,"nova.training.seller-input-ebitda.title","Reported annual EBITDA","nova.training.seller-input-ebitda.body","Annual earnings before interest, tax, depreciation and amortization. Example \u2192 260,000.","nova.training.seller-input-addbacks.title","Verified add-backs","nova.training.seller-input-addbacks.body","Documented costs that will not recur for a new owner. Enter 0 if none. Example \u2192 20,000.","nova.training.seller-input-ownerPay.title","Owner pay in expenses","nova.training.seller-input-ownerPay.body","Your salary and benefits already deducted in reported EBITDA. Enter 0 if EBITDA excludes it. Example \u2192 80,000.","nova.training.seller-input-replacementSalary.title","Replacement leader pay","nova.training.seller-input-replacementSalary.body","Annual cost for someone else to perform your operating role. Example \u2192 95,000.","nova.training.seller-input-lowMultiple.title","Low comparable multiple","nova.training.seller-input-lowMultiple.body","Lower EBITDA multiple supported by similar business sales. Example \u2192 3.","nova.training.seller-input-highMultiple.title","High comparable multiple","nova.training.seller-input-highMultiple.body","Upper EBITDA multiple supported by similar business sales. Example \u2192 5.","nova.training.seller-result-business.title","Business value range","nova.training.seller-result-business.body","Maintainable EBITDA adds verified add-backs and owner pay to reported EBITDA, then subtracts replacement leader pay. The low and high multiples produce the enterprise-value range. Cash, debt and working-capital adjustments are separate. Results appear when the required fields are complete.","nova.training.seller-input-assets.title","Equipment and other tangible assets","nova.training.seller-input-assets.body","Supportable market value of included physical assets. Example \u2192 500,000.","nova.training.seller-input-inventory.title","Saleable inventory","nova.training.seller-input-inventory.body","Usable stock included in the proposed transaction. Example \u2192 180,000.","nova.training.seller-input-receivables.title","Collectible receivables","nova.training.seller-input-receivables.body","Customer balances expected to transfer and be collected. Example \u2192 120,000.","nova.training.seller-input-liabilities.title","Liabilities to be assumed","nova.training.seller-input-liabilities.body","Debt and obligations the buyer would take over. Example \u2192 150,000.","nova.training.seller-result-assets.title","Net asset reference","nova.training.seller-result-assets.body","Included equipment, inventory and collectible receivables minus assumed liabilities gives the net asset reference. This is a separate comparison; adding it to earnings value can double-count assets. Results appear when the required fields are complete.","nova.training.seller-input-price.title","Expected sale price","nova.training.seller-input-price.body","The agreed or proposed gross price before closing adjustments. Example \u2192 1,200,000.","nova.training.seller-input-vendorNote.title","Vendor financing / deferred amount","nova.training.seller-input-vendorNote.body","Part of the price paid after closing. Enter 0 if none. Example \u2192 150,000.","nova.training.seller-input-fees.title","Selling and closing fees","nova.training.seller-input-fees.body","Broker, legal, valuation and other transaction fees. Enter 0 if none. Example \u2192 45,000.","nova.training.seller-input-debtPayoff.title","Debt paid at closing","nova.training.seller-input-debtPayoff.body","Business debt discharged from sale proceeds. Enter 0 if none. Example \u2192 250,000.","nova.training.seller-result-closing.title","Cash at closing","nova.training.seller-result-closing.body","Subtract vendor financing, selling fees and debt paid at closing from the expected price. The result is before tax; holdbacks, earn-outs and working-capital adjustments need separate review. Results appear when the required fields are complete.","nova.training.welcome.title","Hi, I\u2019m Pika.","nova.training.welcome.body",u.T,"nova.training.seller-home.title","Your next chapter starts here","nova.training.seller-home.body",u.y4,"nova.training.seller-value.title","Explore your asking price","nova.training.seller-value.body",u.rf,"nova.training.seller-plan.title","A plan for your transfer path","nova.training.seller-plan.body",u.eu,"nova.training.seller-team.title","Bring the right people together","nova.training.seller-team.body",u.e9,"nova.training.seller-resources.title","Explore support programs"